WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:11.343
Chat is where your team talks, and where a conversation can become a ticket or a doc. In this video, you’ll use a channel, send a direct message, and turn messages into a ticket.

00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:18.513
Open Chat. There’s a channel for each store, crew, or project, and your direct messages underneath.

00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:24.791
New channel makes one for a store, a crew, or a project, and Channel settings chooses who’s in it.

00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:30.076
Messages have reactions and photos. A ticket mentioned in chat links straight to it.

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:40.496
Direct messages are just between the two of you, like swapping a shift. New message starts one with anyone in the company, and chat works the same on your phone.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:45.776
Something needs doing? Click Select messages, and pick the ones that matter.

00:00:46.233 --> 00:00:52.079
Then click Make ticket. Pick the location and the ticket type, and the conversation goes along with it.

00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:59.339
Create it, and the messages link to the ticket they became. Make doc works the same way, for a write-up in Spaces.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:07.843
You can also ask Assist to sum up a channel, or what was decided. Chat is off until your System Admin turns it on in Modules.

